<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bernardo Buontalenti</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1531–<a href="/years/1608">1608</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bernardo Buontalenti was a Florentine architect, engineer, stage designer and artist in the service of the Medici grand dukes. He designed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/forte-di-belvedere">Forte di Belvedere</a> and the Medici villa at Pratolino, completed the Uffizi with its Tribuna, built the Grotta Grande in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boboli-gardens">Boboli Gardens</a> and drew the plan of the new <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/livorno">Livorno</a>. He also staged the lavish court festivals of 1589 that helped prepare the way for opera.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bernardo-buontalenti.jpg" alt="Bernardo Buontalenti" width="320" height="433" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Pietro Antonio Pazzi · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bernardo_Buontalenti_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Florence was overlooked by the Fortezza da Basso, begun under Alessandro in 1534, and by the Forte di Belvedere, designed by <b>Bernardo Buontalenti</b> for Ferdinando I in the 1590s.</blockquote><a href="/empire/grand-duchy-of-tuscany">Grand Duchy of Tuscany · Military</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/florence">Florence</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/italy">Italy</a>. Died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/florence">Florence</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/italy">Italy</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=43.77,11.25&amp;year=1581" aria-label="Florence on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4820 613 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Bernardo Buontalenti"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5270 883h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5270 883h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=43.77,11.25&amp;year=1581">What was here in 1581? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
